It is Saturday.
I go into a large shop in the city centre.
In here it is very warm.
I take off my thin jacket.
I pack the jacket into my shopping bag.
I need a warm jacket or a thick winter coat.
I look by the winter clothes and find a heavy, dark green coat.
It is size thirty-eight.
I look at the price tag.
The coat costs one hundred and twenty Euro.
I put the beautiful coat on right here in the aisle.
It is long and very warm.
It is not cheap, but I am buying it.
I take the coat off again.
I carry it over my arm.
